# Keep the build context small: the Dockerfile does `COPY . /workspace/...`,
# so anything not excluded here is sent to the daemon and baked into the image.

# Credentials and key material.
#
# This block mirrors the credential entries in .gitignore, and has to exist separately from them:
# .gitignore keeps these OUT OF GIT, which is exactly why they are present as untracked files in a
# working tree — and `COPY . /workspace/cdf-anomalygen` below sends the whole context, so without
# these patterns a developer's .env is baked into a layer of an image published to a registry.
# A credential in a published layer is disclosed to everyone who pulls it and survives deletion in
# a later layer, so it must never enter the context in the first place.
#
# Keep in step with .gitignore's credential entries.
.env
*.env
.env.*
/credentials
# The live model registry: carries per-endpoint `key:` values. The template
# (endpoints.example.yaml) stays in the context; only the filled-in copy is banned.
scripts/agentic_mask_generation_serving/endpoints.yaml
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
.ssh/
.aws/
.azure/
.gcloud/
.config/gcloud/
.kube/
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.huggingface/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# VCS / CI
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.gitlab-ci.yml
.github

